description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts, in the region "A slice sequence cut short by a capacity refusal never got its attempt either", deliver a reach verdict after the second direct compose call so its execution row can be graded.

REGION. Ground on the comment beginning "A slice sequence cut short by a capacity refusal never got its attempt either", which occurs exactly once in this file. Below it is a second invocation of resolveFeatureCompose, followed by the line that assigns its body to cb. That assignment is the edit site.

THE DEFECT, measured by census. This file invokes resolveFeatureCompose at three separate call sites. Verdict delivery was added at only one of them. Counted on the live substrate over the eight compose executions since that delivery landed: all eight logged a successful trace capture, so every report carried the execution identifier, yet only two rows ever received a reach tag. The other six passed through the two call sites that have no delivery, so their verdicts were never sent and their rows remain permanently ungraded. This is the same defect class as the original: an identifier that exists and is never used, because a sibling call site was missed.

WHAT MAKES THIS SAFE. Both halves are in scope at the insertion point: the report carries the trace store's execution identifier on its execution_id field, and the verdict is the report's ok field. This mirrors exactly the delivery already present at the first call site. It is fire and forget with a bounded timeout and a swallowing catch, so a trace-store problem cannot affect the compose result, and the function's return value is untouched.

Perform exactly one replacement. Find the sole occurrence of this line:
  const cb = compose.body as Record<string, unknown>;

Replace it with these lines:
  const cb = compose.body as Record<string, unknown>;
  try {
    const reachId2 = typeof cb["execution_id"] === "string" ? (cb["execution_id"] as string) : "";
    if (reachId2.length > 0) {
      const reachEndpoint2 = process.env["METABOB_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8080";
      const reachKey2 = process.env["METABOB_API_KEY"] ?? "";
      void fetch(`${reachEndpoint2}/v2/activities/execution-traces/reach`, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", ...(reachKey2 ? { Authorization: `ApiKey ${reachKey2}` } : {}) },
        body: JSON.stringify({ execution_id: reachId2, reached: cb["ok"] === true }),
        signal: AbortSignal.timeout(5000),
      }).catch(() => { /* grading must never affect the compose result */ });
    }
  } catch { /* verdict delivery is best effort */ }

The first line is reproduced verbatim so every downstream use of cb is unchanged. Distinct local names are used so this cannot collide with the delivery block at the earlier call site. No imports are added: fetch is global and the API key is already read from the environment elsewhere in this file.

One replacement, one file, inside the named region. Change nothing else.

